00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.120
Over time, it is highly likely that
you will generate quite a lot of

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.950
files and folders on your computer.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.970
For most modern  computers,  this isn't
an issue as you have high capacity disk

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:15.390
drives, cloud storage or high capacity
removable media where files can be stored.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.160
However, there may still be instances
where you wish to compress files.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:25.140
This could be for archiving into a limited
space, or it may be that you need to send

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.920
some files as an attachment to an email
and compressing them will reduce the

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.350
size of the file that needs to be sent.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.500
So, to compress a folder, I'm going
to demonstrate with the ITQ folder.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.660
So I'll highlight the ITQ folder
and simply select the cog icon

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.780
and then select compress ITQ.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.089
This then is creating a zip file, as
you can see, indicated with the folder

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.870
with the zip  the center of the icon.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.699
So once that's done, I'll just
quickly move that there and that

00:00:58.699 --> 00:00:59.970
has then compressed that folder.

00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:02.940
So just to see how much
it has compressed it by.

00:01:03.345 --> 00:01:08.745
I can highlight the ITQ folder
and select Get Info, which will

00:01:08.745 --> 00:01:10.215
then give me the information.

00:01:10.215 --> 00:01:12.765
So that is 1.8 megabytes in size.

00:01:12.765 --> 00:01:18.375
So the original size was that, and again,
I can highlight the zip file and select

00:01:18.805 --> 00:01:25.425
Get Info and that will then give me
the information on that, which is 1.5

00:01:25.425 --> 00:01:30.044
megabytes, which may not seem much, but if
you bear in mind that you could have quite

00:01:30.044 --> 00:01:33.975
a lot of files and a lot of folders within
there it can save quite a bit of space.

